{"question": "What book am I currently reading?", "evidence": [{"citation": "bbf975fb8bcbcca49ccc955f7315e0b3:37", "text": "I love the idea of making reading a habit loop. I actually do that already, reading before bed every night. I've been averaging 20-30 pages a night, and some nights I've stayed up way too late reading 50-60 pages in one sitting. Do you have any recommendations for book tracking apps or websites, like Goodreads, to help me stay organized and on top of my reading goals?"}, {"citation": "1db64ae4c4ea6cd39d7833bb163ee897:10", "text": "I'm trying to figure out how to fit more reading time into my daily routine. Do you have any tips on how to prioritize reading when life gets busy? By the way, I'm currently devouring "The Seven Husbands of Evelyn Hugo" and it's hard to put down!"}, {"citation": "d0944154c42940b65bd0d87f583ece97:18", "text": "I'm glad you mentioned the Indie Next List. I've been meaning to check it out. I've been trying to support more indie authors and bookstores lately.

By the way, have you heard about the Book of the Month Club? I've been thinking of joining it, but I'm not sure if it's worth it. Do you have any experience with it?"}, {"citation": "82750a4fde5c13ab6e4b3aba36380b0c:1", "text": "I've actually already started a book club with some friends, and our first meeting is scheduled for next weekend. We're going to discuss "The Last House Guest" by Megan Miranda, which I've already read and really enjoyed."}, {"citation": "9f9dd0732318dfb2e4383b193ec362a4:23", "text": "I think I'll check out Libib and StoryGraph. I'm actually curious about tracking my reading speed and comprehension, so maybe BookNerd will be a good option too. 

By the way, I've been thinking about starting a book club with some friends. Do you have any tips on how to organize and run a successful book club?"}]}
